<title>INDIA: Canon to set up $7.0 mln plant in India.</title>
<headline>Canon to set up $7.0 mln plant in India.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Office-equipment maker Canon Inc is in the process of setting up a $7.0 million photocopier plant in India, the Press Trust of India reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The news agency quoted Tony Fitzgerald, managing director of the Japanese firm's wholly-owned Indian subsidiary, as saying that Bangalore and Delhi were the leading contenders among the possible site for the plant.</p>
<p>Canon recieved permission to set up a fully-owned subsidiary in August 1996, with a total investment of up to $9 million.</p>
<p>--New Delhi Newsroom +91 11 301 2024</p>
